<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04ZG">Example <span data-tag="04ZG">1.1.1.6</span>.</a> Let $S_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial set and let $e \in S_{\bullet }$ be an edge of $S_{\bullet }$. Then $s = d^{1}_{1}(e)$ is a vertex of $S_{\bullet }$ which we refer to as the <em>source</em> of $e$, and $t = d^{1}_{0}(e)$ is a vertex of $S_{\bullet }$ which we refer to as the <em>target</em> of $e$. We will sometimes write $e: x \rightarrow y$ to indicate that $e$ is an edge of $S_{\bullet }$ having source vertex $x$ and target vertex $y$. </p>
